  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As the title says, Very Poor avatars should be allowed in the marketplace (or if they are already, make them actually findable). I get why someone outside of the avatar creation ecosystem may think that not promoting very poor performance avis is a good idea, but as someone who is in that ecosystem, it is not only very clearly not a good idea, but actively preventing the in-game marketplace from being an effective money-maker for vrc, or a good place to host avatars for creators.\n\nIf you want proof, go to any online marketplace for avis, you'll find that 99% of the avis that people ACTUALLY buy are very poor. This is because it is very difficult to make an avatar with both a better performance rank than very poor AND enough features to be worth buying. It is nearly impossible to make a decent avi that has clothing options and is below the strict limits for even poor rank (mainly since, for some reason, the poly count limit stops going up after good).",
